    "title": "Five OSHA Compliance Priorities For Wide-Format Print Providers - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Gabby Houck ,\n1 days ago The following article was originally published by Wide-format Impressions. To read more of their content, subscribe to their newsletter, Wide-Format Impressions. For wide-format print service providers, and the industry as a whole, OSHA compliance is not limited to a binder on a shelf. It reaches into the cords powering equipment, the bottles used during cleanup, the guards surrounding moving parts, and the response to an employee who reports an odor. In a conversation with Wide-format Impressions, Gary Jones, vice president of Environmental, Health, and Safety Affairs for PRINTING United Alliance, outlined recurring risks and practical steps print service providers (PSPs) can take to address them. Read full article",
